{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Calculated_Gamble","to":"Calculated Gamble"},{"from":"Core_Surge","to":"Core Surge"},{"from":"Bouncing_Flask","to":"Bouncing Flask"},{"from":"Reach_Heaven","to":"Reach Heaven"},{"from":"Sever_Soul","to":"Sever Soul"},{"from":"Reinforced_Body","to":"Reinforced Body"},{"from":"Genetic_Algorithm","to":"Genetic Algorithm"},{"from":"Cloak_and_Dagger","to":"Cloak and Dagger"},{"from":"Empty_Body","to":"Empty Body"},{"from":"Defend_(Defect)","to":"Defend (Defect)"},{"from":"Pressure_Points","to":"Pressure Points"}],"pages":{"1819":{"pageid":1819,"ns":0,"title":"Anger","revisions":[{"revid":50389,"parentid":35918,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Anger\n|Image       = Red-Anger.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (6;8) damage.<br>Add a copy of this card into your discard pile.\n}}\n{{C|Anger}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (8 if upgraded) damage, and adds a copy of itself into your discard pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Anger}} works well with any draw, most notably with {{R|Unceasing Top}}.\n* The created copy will be upgraded if the original copy was upgraded, or if {{C|Master Reality}} is active.\n* Playing it multiple times, through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, will make multiple copies as well.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Anger card buff: 5 -> 6 damage. Upgraded 7 -> 8 damage.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Anger card damage buffed by 1.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1963":{"pageid":1963,"ns":0,"title":"Bouncing Flask","revisions":[{"revid":56785,"parentid":56031,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bouncing Flask\n|Image       = Green-BouncingFlask.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Apply 3 {{BD|Poison}} to a random enemy (3;4) times.\n|GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}\n{{C|Bouncing Flask}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}, meaning it activates 3 (4 if this card is upgraded) times.\n\n* {{C|Bouncing Flask}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}, {{C|Envenom}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}}.\n** However, as Bouncing Flask applies Poison multiple times in a single card play, it can be very effective at clearing {{BD|Artifact}} for your other {{BD|Poison}} cards.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Bouncing Flask no longer loses bounces to dead enemies.\n\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\nAdding null check for Bouncing Flask VFX to prevent odd crashes.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1822":{"pageid":1822,"ns":0,"title":"Calculated Gamble","revisions":[{"revid":56376,"parentid":55397,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Calculated Gamble\n| Image       = Green-CalculatedGamble.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Discard your hand,<br>then draw that many cards.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw, Discard, Exhaust\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Calculated Gamble}} is a 0 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] all cards in your hand, and then draws cards equal to the amount of cards [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this way. {{C|Calculated Gamble}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself, if it is not upgraded.\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}} is a powerful source of draw, and its [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] effect synergises with several [[Silent]] cards and relics:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* [[Keywords#Discard|Discarding]] {{C|Tactician}} or {{C|Reflex}} will immediately activate their effects.\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} is discounted by X {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' this turn, where X is the number of cards discarded.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}} will now refund 2 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if also played this turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} will grant 3 {{KW|Block}} per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Tingsha}} will deal 3 damage to a random enemy per card [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n* {{R|Hovering Kite}} will generate 1 {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' if this is the first time a card has been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] this turn.\n\n=== Neutral === \n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}} can also be used to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] cards with end-of-turn effects, like {{C|Burn}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} such as {{C|Regret}}.\n\n* {{C|Shiv}}-generating cards such as {{C|Blade Dance}} can be played to increase the player's hand size before playing {{C|Calculated Gamble}} to then increase the number of cards drawn. This does mean, however, that {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} may be redrawn on future turns.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Since {{C|Calculated Gamble}} [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] your entire hand, it may discard {{KW|Ethereal}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} cards that would otherwise automatically {{KW|Exhaust}} at the end of your turn, such as {{C|Dazed}} or {{C|Void}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card depicts a \"false\" die, as a fair die can never have both the 3-side and the 4-side visible. They should be on opposite sides. This could be an oversight, or dice in the Spire universe simply work differently.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Calculated Gamble card nerfed.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1949":{"pageid":1949,"ns":0,"title":"Cloak and Dagger","revisions":[{"revid":56773,"parentid":56772,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Cloak and Dagger\n| Image       = Green-CloakandDagger.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain 6 {{KW|Block}}.<br>Add (1;2) {{C|Shiv|(Shiv;Shivs)}} into your hand.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Shiv\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Shiv}}\n{{C|Cloak and Dagger}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 6 {{KW|Block}} and adds 1 {{C|Shiv}} (2 {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} if upgraded) to your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies === \n* The damage of each {{C|Shiv}} will be increased by the amount of {{BD|Accuracy}} you have, which can be obtained from {{C|Accuracy}}.\n\n* {{R|Wrist Blade}} increases the damage of every {{C|Shiv}} by 4.\n\n* Anything that benefits from {{KW|Exhaust}} will be triggered by playing {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Shiv}} generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Title capitalization for Cloak And Dagger -> Cloak and Dagger.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Cloak and Dagger no longer appears in the card match event before it is unlocked, instead there is always a copy of Neutralize.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1915":{"pageid":1915,"ns":0,"title":"Core Surge","revisions":[{"revid":56638,"parentid":55707,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Core Surge\n| Image       = Blue-CoreSurge.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (11;15) damage.<br>Gain 1 {{BD|Artifact}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Artifact, Exhaust\n}}\n{{C|Core Surge}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 11(15) damage, {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}, and applies the {{BD|Artifact}} [[Buff]] on the player, preventing the next [[Debuff]] they would receive.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\nCore Surge can synergize with anything that applies a [[Debuff]] to the player as a drawback by negating the drawback.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Reprogram}}\n* {{C|Biased Cognition}}\n* {{C|Hyperbeam}}\n\n==== b) Potions ====\n* {{P|Flex Potion}}\n* {{P|Speed Potion}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Temporary {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Dexterity}} boosts such as those from {{P|Flex Potion}} give two separate effects; the buff itself, as well as a debuff {{BD|Strength Down}} or {{BD|Dexterity Down}} that takes the buff away at the end of the turn. If the player has {{BD|Artifact}} when using one of these effects, it will negate the {{BD|Strength Down}} or {{BD|Dexterity Down}} debuff, causing the player to receive permanent {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will not negate {{C|Blasphemy}}'s \"Die next turn,\" since {{BD|Blasphemer}} is coded as a [[Buff]] rather than as a [[Debuff]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2430":{"pageid":2430,"ns":0,"title":"Dazed","revisions":[{"revid":56960,"parentid":55730,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dazed\n|Image       = Colorless-Dazed.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Status\n|Rarity      = Status\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>{{KW|Ethereal}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Unplayable, Ethereal\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Ethereal}}\n{{C|Dazed}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|Common:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} Card.\n\n== Obtaining Dazed ==\nPlaying {{C|Reckless Charge}} will add a {{C|Dazed}} to the player's draw pile.\n\nThe following enemies can give the player {{C|Dazed}}:\n* {{M|Chosen}}\n** {{Int|Chosen|Hex}} - Applies {{BD|Hex}}.\n** {{BD|Hex}} - Whenever you play a non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card, shuffle X {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.\n* {{M|Repulsor}}\n** {{Int|Repulsor|Daze}} - Adds 2 {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.\n* {{M|Sentry}}\n** {{Int|Sentry|Bolt}} - Adds 2({{Asc|18|3}}) {{C|Dazed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Deca}}\n** {{Int|Deca|Beam}} - Adds 2 {{C|Dazed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Corrupt Heart}}\n** {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}} - Adds 1 {{C|Dazed}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Triggers the damage from {{C|Fire Breathing}}.\n* Draws cards with {{C|Evolve}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Second Wind}} and triggers its {{KW|Block}} gain.\n* Can be {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} with {{R|Medical Kit}} to trigger exhaust synergies such as {{C|Feel No Pain}} or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}, or will {{KW|Exhaust}} on its own at the end of your turn.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} by {{C|Sever Soul}} since it's not an {{QueryLink|Cards|Type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Prevents {{C|Clash}} from being played.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Dazed and Clumsy now exhaust even if retained via Well Laid Plans (all Ethereal cards).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Dazed card is now Ethereal. Doesn't really impact gameplay.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1490":{"pageid":1490,"ns":0,"title":"Defend (Defect)","revisions":[{"revid":56345,"parentid":50547,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Defend (Defect)\n| DisplayName = Defend\n| Image       = Blue-Defend.png\n| Color       = Blue\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Basic\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Defend (Defect)|Defend}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 (8 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}.\n\nThis page is for the Defect's version of Defend, go here for {{C|Defend (Ironclad)}}, {{C|Defend (Silent)}}, {{C|Defend (Watcher)}}\n\n== Obtaining Defend ==\nThe [[Defect]] starts with 4 copies of {{C|Defend (Defect)|Defend}} in their deck. It cannot be obtained through regular card rewards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2277":{"pageid":2277,"ns":0,"title":"Empty Body","revisions":[{"revid":54826,"parentid":50640,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Empty Body\n|Image       = Purple-EmptyBody.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (7;10) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Exit your {{KW|Stance}}.\n}}\n{{C|Empty Body}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 7 (10 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, and makes you exit your current {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When you exit any {{KW|Stance}}, the following will occur:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n** When you exit {{KW|Calm}}, it has the additional effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2013":{"pageid":2013,"ns":0,"title":"Equilibrium","revisions":[{"revid":56792,"parentid":56136,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Equilibrium\n|Image       = Blue-Equilibrium.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (13;16) {{KW|Block}}.<br>{{KW|Retain}} your hand this turn.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n|GivesToPlayer = Block, Equilibrium\n|PowerGives = Retain\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Equilibrium\n|Image        = Icon Equilibrium.png\n|Description  = Retain your hand for X turns.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Duration\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}}\n{{C|Equilibrium}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n* {{C|Equilibrium}} allows {{C|Multi-Cast}} to be saved to evoke an orb at the correct time, perhaps waiting for a {{KW|Dark}} [[Orbs|Orb]] to charge.\n* {{C|Establishment}}, if acquired via {{R|Prismatic Shard}} or {{E|A Note For Yourself}}, will discount every card {{KW|Retain|Retained}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Equilibrium}} is played when the player already has the {{BD|Equilibrium}} buff, its duration will increase. For example, copying {{C|Equilibrium}} with {{C|Echo Form}} will {{KW|Retain}} the player's hand for two turns.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Equilibrium}}'s {{KW|Retain}} effect is redundant with {{R|Runic Pyramid}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{C|Equilibrium}} is internally called Undo.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Equilibrium Power's icon is now the same as Retain Power (used icon for Blur previously).\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\nThis week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\nA new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2053":{"pageid":2053,"ns":0,"title":"Footwork","revisions":[{"revid":55790,"parentid":50512,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Footwork\n|Image       = Green-Footwork.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (2;3) {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Dexterity}}{{C|Footwork}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2134":{"pageid":2134,"ns":0,"title":"Genetic Algorithm","revisions":[{"revid":56170,"parentid":50591,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Genetic Algorithm\n|Image       = Blue-GeneticAlgorithm.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain 1 {{KW|Block}}. Permanently increase this card's {{KW|Block}} by (2;3).<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Genetic Algorithm}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 1 {{KW|Block}} and permanently increases this {{KW|Block}} by 2 (3 if upgraded). {{C|Genetic Algorithm}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When played multiple times, it also permanently scales multiple times, and the consecutive plays already use the scaling from the previous plays. This can be done with {{C|Echo Form}}, {{C|Burst}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}.\n** Notably, this does not work with {{C|Omniscience}}.\n\n* As one of the few cards that has benefits that remain outside of combat, triggering it as often as possible becomes an additional objective within combat. Given that {{C|Genetic Algorithm}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after use, it synergizes with:\n** {{R|Strange Spoon}}, which gives a 50% chance to not {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Genetic Algorithm}} when played, allowing it to be redrawn and used again.\n** {{C|Exhume}}, which can get {{C|Genetic Algorithm}} back once after being played, with the added benefit of putting it directly into your hand.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Automaton's orbs preventing scaling of Genetic Algorithm and Ritual Dagger.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Fix for proper behavior when duplicating cards like Rampage and Genetic Algorithm with effects like Echo Form.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1836":{"pageid":1836,"ns":0,"title":"Offering","revisions":[{"revid":56388,"parentid":53366,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Offering\n| Image       = Red-Offering.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Lose 6 HP.<br>Gain {{Icon|RE}} {{Icon|RE}}.<br>Draw (3;5) cards.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Lose HP, Energy, Exhaust, Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Offering}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It costs 6 HP to play, gives 2 {{Icon|RE}} energy and draws 3 (5 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Offering}} can be used to trigger {{C|Rupture}}, {{R|Runic Cube}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} and {{R|Runic Cube}}, and lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Offering}} can trigger {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}, which could be wasteful, as the combined total draw can exceed the hand size limit.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Offering card is now faster in Fast Mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Adding VFX for Offering card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Offering card nerf: HP Loss increased from 5 -> 6.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Offering card nerf: Self damage increased from 4 -> 5.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Optional UPGRADE_DESCRIPTION added for Pummel, Heavy Blade, Offering, and Reprogram\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Fixed issue where playing cost X cards quickly after energy gain cards failed. Offering -> Whirlwind\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Offering card gets a minor change. HP Loss is now 4. Card draw upgrades from 3 -> 5.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2294":{"pageid":2294,"ns":0,"title":"Pressure Points","revisions":[{"revid":55851,"parentid":55209,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Pressure Points\n|Image       = Purple-PressurePoints.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Apply (8;11) {{BD|Mark}}.<br>ALL enemies lose HP equal to their {{BD|Mark}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Mark\n|Image        = Icon Mark.png\n|Description  = Whenever you play {{C|Pressure Points}}, lose X HP.\n|Type         = Debuffs\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|Pressure Points}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies 8 (11 if upgraded) {{BD|Mark}} to one target, and then '''ALL''' enemies with {{BD|Mark}} lose HP equal to their {{BD|Mark}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with itself, as it increases in effectiveness the more enemies have {{BD|Mark}}, and the more {{BD|Mark}} they have.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* During beta testing for the Watcher, Pressure Points was called Path to Victory. The name change to the current one was suggested by the community in order to make it fit its effect thematically. The internal name for {{C|Pressure Points}} is still Path to Victory.\n** Path to Victory itself was reworked once, with the original effect \"Draw a card and reduce its cost to 0 this turn. Exhaust.\" and would not Exhaust if Upgraded.\n** Path to Victory is a reference to the web serial Worm, in which the character Contessa has the power to see the steps necessary to succeed at any given task, referred to as \"Path to Victory.\"\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2296":{"pageid":2296,"ns":0,"title":"Prostrate","revisions":[{"revid":55909,"parentid":50650,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Prostrate\n|Image       = Purple-Prostrate.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain (2;3) {{BD|Mantra}}. <br>Gain 4 {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Mantra}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Prostrate}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Mantra}} and 4 {{KW|Block}}. When reaching 10 {{BD|Mantra}}, all of it will be removed and you will enter the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Brilliance}} increases in damage whenever you gain {{BD|Mantra}}.\n\n* All {{BD|Mantra}} sources synergize with eachother: {{C|Pray}}, {{C|Worship}}, {{C|Devotion}} and {{R|Damaru}} work well with {{C|Prostrate}}.\n\n* When entering {{KW|Divinity}} if you are not in {{KW|Divinity}} yet, you will gain 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' and switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* While in {{KW|Divinity}}, all damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} is tripled. This does not affect damage from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1930":{"pageid":1930,"ns":0,"title":"Rage","revisions":[{"revid":56755,"parentid":55911,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Rage\n|Image       = Red-Rage.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Whenever you play an Attack this turn, gain (3;5) {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Rage\n|PowerGives = Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Rage\n| Image        = Icon Anger.png\n| Description  = Whenever you play an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} this turn, gain X {{KW|Block}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = Removed\n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Rage}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Rage}}, which gives that amount of {{KW|Block}} every time an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} is played this turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Rage}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 22: Testing the Third Character'''\n** Fixing crashes for ZHS when viewing Rage card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** Rage card gets a buff, cost 1 -> 0. Block 4 -> 3.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2315":{"pageid":2315,"ns":0,"title":"Reach Heaven","revisions":[{"revid":53294,"parentid":50675,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reach Heaven\n|Image       = Purple-ReachHeaven.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (10;15) damage. Shuffle a {{C|Through Violence}} into your draw pile.\n}}\n{{C|Reach Heaven}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 10 damage (15 when upgraded) and shuffles a {{C|Through Violence}} into the player's draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n\n* Having {{C|Master Reality}} in play before playing {{C|Reach Heaven}} will create an upgraded {{C|Through Violence}}+.\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Through Violence ==\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Through Violence\n|Image       = Colorless-ThroughViolence.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Deal (20;30) damage. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Through Violence}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 20 (30 if upgraded) damage and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* The combined names of {{C|Reach Heaven}} {{C|Through Violence}} is a reference to the 2013 webcomic Kill Six Billion Demons<ref>https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Webcomic/KillSixBillionDemons</ref> where the phrase \"Reach heaven through violence\" (and many variations) are common proverbs mentioned throughout the story.\n** This originally came from Sermon Fifteen of The 36 Lessons of Vivec from the 2002 video game [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Elder_Scrolls_III:_Morrowind The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind], developed by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bethesda_Game_Studios Bethesda], where Vivec is quoted ''\"Reach heaven by violence\"''<ref>https://en.uesp.net/wiki/Morrowind:36_Lessons_of_Vivec,_Sermon_15</ref>.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2210":{"pageid":2210,"ns":0,"title":"Reinforced Body","revisions":[{"revid":55921,"parentid":50600,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reinforced Body\n|Image       = Blue-ReinforcedBody.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = -1\n|Description = Gain (7;9) {{KW|Block}} X times.\n}}\n{{C|Reinforced Body}} is an X {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|SKill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits '''X''' times from {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} makes {{C|Reinforced Body}} apply 2 more times, regardless of the amount of {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' used to play it.\n* If played using {{P|Distilled Chaos}}, {{C|Havoc}}, or {{C|Omniscience}}, it will play for the full current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' without actually using any.\n* Can be used with 0 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' to advance {{R|Ink Bottle}} or {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{C|Reinforced Body}} is duplicated with an effect such as a {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Burst}}, the value of '''X''' will also be used for the copy.\n* Being an X-cost, {{C|Reinforced Body}} can be {{C|Recycle|Recycled}} to double the current {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy'''.\n* It will not count as a 0-cost card for {{C|Scrape}} or {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Corruption and other cost reducing cards no longer make X cost cards like Transmutation and Malaise display cost 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2263":{"pageid":2263,"ns":0,"title":"Seek","revisions":[{"revid":50628,"parentid":36279,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Seek\n|Image       = Blue-Seek.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Put (1;2) (card;cards) from your draw pile into your hand.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Seek}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to choose 1 card (2 cards if upgraded) from your draw pile to place into your hand, after which this {{C|Seek}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Seek}} is removed from your hand before the selected card is added to your hand, meaning that even with a full hand {{C|Seek}} will be able to replace itself with the desired card.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If you have no cards in your draw pile when playing this card, it will simply {{KW|Exhaust}} without having an effect. If you only have 1 card in your draw pile when playing an upgraded {{C|Seek}}, you will only get that 1 card.\n\n* If your hand is full when playing an upgraded {{C|Seek}}, the card you selected first will be added to your hand and the second card will be added to your discard pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Seek card now organizes cards by rarity and alphabetically.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1848":{"pageid":1848,"ns":0,"title":"Sever Soul","revisions":[{"revid":56396,"parentid":55496,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Sever Soul\n| Image       = Red-SeverSoul.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = {{KW|Exhaust}} all non-Attack cards in your hand.<br>Deal (16;22) damage.\n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Sever Soul}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 16 (22 if upgraded) damage, and {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} all non-{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards in your hand. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Sever Soul}} has {{KW|Exhaust}}-synergy with {{C|Dark Embrace}}, {{C|Feel No Pain}}, {{R|Charon's Ashes}} and {{R|Dead Branch}}, and can reliably {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Sentinel}}.\n* Sever Soul can be used to get rid of unwanted cards in hand, such as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} cards.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The amount of cards {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} through {{C|Sever Soul}} has no effect on the effectiveness of the card, even if no cards get {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} at all.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Sever Soul+ card buffed. Damage increased from 20 -> 22.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2077":{"pageid":2077,"ns":0,"title":"Streamline","revisions":[{"revid":50569,"parentid":36225,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Streamline\n|Image       = Blue-Streamline.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (15;20) damage.<br>Reduce this card's cost by 1 this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Streamline}} is a 2 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Playing {{C|Enlightenment}} and then playing  {{C|Streamline}} will immediately reduce its cost to '''0''' {{Icon|BE}}.\n* Playing {{C|Streamline}} with any duplicating effect like {{C|Echo Form}} or {{R|Necronomicon}} will immediately reduce its cost to '''0''' {{Icon|BE}}.\n\n==== While at 0{{Icon|BE}}cost ====\n* Will be pulled back by {{C|All for One}}.\n* Can be drawn into by {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}